        pitfall: "Social services calls that start as benefit inquiries can reveal crisis situations: a parent calling about SNAP eligibility mentions that her partner hit her child last night. The agent must recognize this as a mandatory reporting situation, not a benefits question. Train every social services agent as a mandatory reporter and build a one-button crisis escalation that connects to child protective services or law enforcement immediately."
